# Complete the credential and side-effect threat model

## Goal

Define how mailbox authority is acquired, held, constrained, observed, and
revoked before real credentials are accepted.

## Required work

- Model the user, AI client, MCP process, Bridge, operating system, and Proton.
- Model the visible browser/Playwright boundary, credential store, remote
  operator, remote client, and tenant boundaries.
- Define credential storage and zeroization expectations.
- Specify structural redaction and safe diagnostic fields.
- Define confirmations, idempotency, retries, cancellation, and recovery.
- Bound attachment paths, sizes, content types, and output destinations.

## Acceptance criteria

- Threats cover disclosure, confused deputy behavior, prompt injection,
  unintended send, deletion, replay, attachment traversal, and log leakage.
- Read, reversible, external-side-effect, and destructive tools have distinct
  policy.
- Permanent deletion remains disabled until separately proven.
- Security tests contain no real account data.
- Session expiry, logout, account switching, remote revocation, and credential
  store failure have explicit safe states.

